rability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.14221774487893243,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.15159472676090768,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":1161.9166666666667,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.28628,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.154,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":15.4,"pf":[],"description_full":"Lyell Immunopharma, Inc., a clinical-stage cell therapy company, develops chimeric antigen receptor (CAR) T-cell product candidates for patients with hematologic malignancies and solid tumors. The company's lead product candidate include rondecabtagene autoleucel, an autologous dual-targeting CD19/CD20 CAR T-cell therapy in development, which is in pivotal PiNACLE trial in the 3L+ setting and in a Phase 1/2 clinical trial in the 2L setting, as well as a second pivotal trial, PiNACLE-H2H, which is a Phase 3 head-to-head CAR T cell therapy randomized controlled trial of ronde-cel for LBCL in the 2L setting for the treatment of large B-cell lymphoma; and LYL273, a GCC-targeted CAR T-cell product candidate enhanced with CD19 CAR expression and controlled cytokine release designed to improve CAR T-cell expansion, immune cell infiltration, and cancer cell killing in the hostile solid tumor microenvironment, which is in Phase 1 clinical trial for the treatment of refractory metastatic colorectal cancer. The company develops therapies using various approaches, such as c-Jun overexpression and NR4A3 gene knockout, to endow functional resistance to exhaustion; Epi-R to generate population of stem-like T cells with reduced exhaustion and improved proliferation and antitumor activity; and CD62L positive enrichment to generate CAR T cells with enhanced antitumor activity. Lyell Immunopharma, Inc. was incorporated in 2018 and is headquartered in South San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Lynn  Seely M.D., Ph.D. | Principal Executive Officer, President, CEO & Director | Age 66 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 161 people. Revenue per employee of $224 ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue falling 76%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $260K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5044\u00d7 revenue per employee (very high relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Lyell Immunopharma, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $352M market cap on $36,000 of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -92% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -129% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $151M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Net dilution runs at 14.2% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 116192% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 29% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-6.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 748344% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (85% sell ratio) over the past year","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.154},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 108% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Large open-market insider purchases (net $49.8M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Critical Analysis: Century Therapeutics (NASDAQ:IPSC) and Lyell Immunopharma (NASDAQ:LYEL)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolni